      },
      "content": "Thinking LMs are sentient is the flip side of thinking nonhuman animals aren't sentient. We're so attuned to language as a signal for sentience that we can't conceive of unpairing sentience from linguistic competence. So we feel LMs are people, but tool-using crows and octopuses as meat.",
